@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Logical-seat edge integration regression
+
+Runs a private nested compositor in a hidden workspace, with a second headless
+output and synthetic Wayland devices. It never injects into the parent desktop
+or takes physical input devices. Requires Python/PyGObject GTK3, Wayland client
+and xkbcommon development files, and an already-built optimized native fork.
+
+```sh
+caelestia-build -- tests/multiseat/input-client/build.sh
+MULTISEAT_REPORT=/tmp/edge-results.json python tests/multiseat/test_edges.py
+```
+
+Override `NATIVE_TEST_BINARY` to check another build. The regression pushes both
+cursors against all edges, checks the midpoint of absolute secondary-seat input,
+and puts a primary-seat floating window across the display boundary. Motion from
+the laptop must never enter that foreign window. Normal mode retains the shared
+layout; ownership filters are active only when logical seats are enabled.
